    <p class="font-body text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed max-w-xl mb-8">
      ostk views humans and LLMs as two distinct execution resources. The <code class="text-primary">CpuDriver</code> trait abstracts this boundary—allowing the kernel to route commands without needing to know whether it communicates with a TTY or an API:
    </p>

